{
  "name": "Restorative Reagents (Alchemist)",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You can incorporate restorative reagents into some of your works:</p><ul><li>Whenever a creature drinks an experimental elixir you created, the creature gains temporary hit points equal to 2d6 + your Intelligence modifier (minimum of 1 temporary hit point).</li><li>You can cast Lesser Restoration without expending a spell slot and without preparing the spell, provided you have alchemist's supplies on your person. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</li></ul>",
